# Only the built site is deployed.
#
# This repository is an Expo app plus a static marketing site, and the Vercel
# project has buildCommand: null with outputDirectory: website/dist. Everything
# below is either already copied into dist or irrelevant to a static site, so
# uploading it would just slow the deploy down.
#
# The most important line is website/public/downloads: the universal APK is
# 110.1 MB and a Vercel Hobby deployment caps static uploads at 100 MB. The APK
# is served from a GitHub release instead, so the binary must never be uploaded.

# The APK (hosted on a GitHub release; see website/site.config.mjs apkPath)
website/public/downloads
website/dist/downloads

# Build output is generated from these; dist already contains the copies.
website/public/assets
website/public/*.png
website/src
website/*.mjs
website/README.md

# The Expo application itself is not part of a static marketing site.
src
assets
images
supabase
scripts
docs
.expo
ios
android
.expo-shared

# Tooling / CI noise
.github
.claude
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo